29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #GPU is fine again — same header, CUDA:0 detected. This error is about the dataset/source,
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #not the model or drivers.
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #What it means: Ultralytics built the image list, got zero usable entries, and something incremented
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #the internal cursor past the end, so `__len__` returned a negative number. In practice this almost
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #always means the `source` resolved to something with no valid images in it — an empty directory, a
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #`.txt` whose lines aren’t real image paths, or a path that no longer exists but no longer raises
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #`FileNotFoundError` (e.g. an empty dir).
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #`count.py` ran fine earlier, so the model and env are good. Only the loader is unhappy.
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #I need three things:
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #cat run.sh
29cef749 [deepseek-flash] #
