2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.011 1.365MB 14.45s
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #Both files read cleanly. Here is what stands out relative to what I would consider the "common"
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #published versions of each.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #Discord (`discordopenapi.json`)
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #- OpenAPI 3.1.0, spec version `10`, explicitly labelled "Preview" — so it tracks the
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #current developer docs rather than a frozen release.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #- Endpoint surface is broader than the classic bot-API set. Notable additions:
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/lobbies` and `/lobbies/{lobby_id}/...` (create/join, channel-linking, members, messages,
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #moderation metadata)
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/partner-sdk/token`, `/partner-sdk/token/bot`,
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #`/partner-sdk/provisional-accounts/unmerge[/bot]`
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/invites/{code}/target-users` (CSV get/put, bulk add/delete, job status)
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/guilds/{guild_id}/requests` and `.../requests/{request_id}` (join requests)
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `.../scheduled-events/.../exceptions` and `.../users/counts`
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/channels/{channel_id}/threads/search`, `/channels/{channel_id}/voice-status`
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `/applications/{application_id}/activity-instances/{instance_id}`
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #- Schema-side novelties worth flagging:
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `flags_new` as a string alongside the integer `flags` on applications/users.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `vibegrations_project_id` on application responses.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `primary_guild`, `collectibles` / nameplates, `avatar_decoration_data` on user objects.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `shared_client_theme` (request + response) on messages.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - `message_snapshots` and a `MessageSnapshotResponse` wrapping `MinimalContentMessageResponse`.
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #  - New component types in `MessageComponentTypes`: `LABEL` (18), `FILE_UPLOAD` (19), `RADIO_GROUP`
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #(21), `CHECKBOX_GROUP` (22), `CHECKBOX` (23), plus `CONTAINER`, `SECTION`, `TEXT_DISPLAY`,
2a1ae6da [deepseek-flash] #`MEDIA_GALLERY`, `FILE`, `SEPARATOR`, `THUMBNAIL`.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - `InteractionCallbackTypes` includes `LAUNCH_ACTIVITY` (12) and
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`SOCIAL_LAYER_SKU_PURCHASE_ELIGIBILITY` (13).
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - `ApplicationFormPartial` now carries `event_webhooks_status`, `event_webhooks_url`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`event_webhooks_types`.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - `ApplicationIdentityProviderAuthType` covers OIDC, Epic, Steam, Unity, Apple, PlayStation, and
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #Discord bot-issued tokens.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #Godot (`godot.json`)
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #- Metadata is descriptive only (name/version/copyright/license/latest/curator) — it is a class
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #index, not a method/property signature dump.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #- `"latest": "4.7.2"` is well ahead of the 4.3/4.4 line most people are on, so treat the class
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #lists as forward-looking.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #- Category split (`variant`, `globals`, `node`, `object`, `resource`, `editor`) is clean and
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #internally consistent; `object` is a superset that also pulls in editor classes, which is worth
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #knowing if you plan to drive codegen off it.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #- Items that signal newer or less-common engine work:
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - Modifier3D family: `AimModifier3D`, `ConvertTransformModifier3D`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`CopyTransformModifier3D`, `LookAtModifier3D`, `LimitAngularVelocityModifier3D`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`RetargetModifier3D`.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - IK expansion: `ChainIK3D`, `IterateIK3D`, `JacobianIK3D`, `FABRIK3D`, `CCDIK3D`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`SplineIK3D`, `TwoBoneIK3D`, plus `JointLimitation3D` / `JointLimitationCone3D`.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - Spring bone stack: `SpringBoneSimulator3D`, `SpringBoneCollision3D` and its
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #capsule/plane/sphere variants.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - Rendering internals surfaced as classes: `RenderData`, `RenderScene`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`RDAccelerationStructureGeometry`, `RDHitGroup`, `FramebufferCacheRD`, `UniformSetCacheRD`,
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #`BlitMaterial`, `DrawableTexture2D`.
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #  - OpenXR is heavily represented: spatial capabilities
2a1ae6db [deepseek-flash] #(`OpenXRSpatialCapabilityConfiguration`, `OpenXRSpatialComponent`),
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #`OpenXRFrameSynthesisExtension`, `OpenXRFutureExtension`, `OpenXRAndroidThreadSettingsExtension`,
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #tracker variants.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #  - Networking/IO additions: `StreamPeerUDS`, `UDPServer`, `UDSServer`, `IPUnix`, `WebRTC*`
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #extension classes, `SceneCacheInterface`, `SceneRPCInterface`, `SceneReplicationInterface`.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #  - Movie writers: `MovieWriterMJPEG`, `MovieWriterOGV`, `MovieWriterPNGWAV` (base
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #`MovieWriter`).
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #  - UI additions: `FoldableContainer`, `FoldableGroup`, `VirtualJoystick`,
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #`StatusIndicator`, `ColorPalette`, `EditorDock`.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #  - `GodotInstance`, `GodotPhysicsServer2D/3D`, `NavigationServer2DManager/3DManager` — useful
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #hooks if you are embedding or extending.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #  - `ShaderInclude` / `ShaderIncludeDB` are present as first-class resources.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #Cross-file observation
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #The two specs are at very different levels of granularity: Discord is a full request/response
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #contract with auth, headers, and error models, whereas the Godot file is an enumerable taxonomy
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #with light per-class notes (`guide`). If `biblispec` expects a uniform shape, the Godot entry will
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #likely need either a companion signature file or a documented "index-only" category. Nothing in
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #either file is malformed on inspection.
2a1ae6dc [deepseek-flash] #
