2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.016 1.373MB 31.58s
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #The script is a faithful generator for the `godot.json` we looked at, with a couple of divergences
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #and a few small things worth flagging.
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #It reproduces the earlier file closely
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8ef [deepseek-flash] #- `variant` list, `globals`, category ordering, tab-indented JSON, and the `is_parent_class`
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #semantics all match the observed output. In particular, `ClassDB.is_parent_class` returns true when
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #the two names are equal, which is why `Node`, `Resource`, and `Object` appear in their own category
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #lists — that is intentional, not an accident of the loop.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- `get_variant_names` produces the same sorted list (including `Variant` inserted via the guard, so
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #no duplicate from `type_string`).
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- `is_editor_class` covers every entry in the earlier `editor` array: all of them begin with
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #`Editor` or `ResourceImporter`.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #Where it diverges from the earlier JSON
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- The earlier file has `"version": "0.2.0"` and a `"guide"` section describing `Node` and `Node2D`.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #The script emits `"version": "0.1.0"` and no `guide`. So either the earlier file was hand-edited,
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #or a newer revision of this script exists.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- The earlier `"curator"` is `"Curated by nitrologic"`; the script emits `"nitrologic"`. Cosmetic,
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #but worth aligning.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #Small points
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- The triple-quoted string after `extends SceneTree` is not a docstring — GDScript has no docstring
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #mechanism, and a bare string at script scope is an unused expression (warning, not error).
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #Idiomatic GDScript documentation uses `##` line comments. If the intent is documentation, that is
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #the cleaner choice.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- `str(registered_class)` is redundant: `ClassDB.get_class_list()` already returns a
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #`PackedStringArray` of `String`. Harmless, but it hides the type.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- `ClassDB.get_class_list()` only includes editor-registered classes when the editor-enabled binary
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #is used. Running this via the non-editor template (or a stripped export) will silently drop the
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #whole `editor` array rather than error. Worth an explicit assertion or a printed warning if
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #`editors.is_empty()`.
2a1af8f0 [deepseek-flash] #- `is_editor_class` is a name-prefix heuristic. It happens to match the current class list, but any
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #future editor class not prefixed `Editor`/`ResourceImporter` (and there is no public `ClassDB`
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #query for "editor-only") will be missed. A short comment noting the heuristic would help a future
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #reader.
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #- `Engine.get_version_info().string` would give the same `major.minor.patch` string; the manual
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #formatting is fine, but the dict field already exists.
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #- `_init` on a `SceneTree` script does work for `--script` invocation because the script instance
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #is constructed before the main loop starts; `quit()` then takes effect on the first iteration. If
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #you ever move to `extends MainLoop`, the virtual to override is `_initialize`/`_process`, not
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #`_init`.
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #Suggestion
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #If you want the script to emit the `0.2.0` shape, the changes are: bump the literal version, add a
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #static `guide` dictionary, and set `curator` to the descriptive string. All three are plain
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #dictionary edits in `build_schema_dictionary`. Say the word and I can draft them.
2a1af8f1 [deepseek-flash] #
