2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.002 4.147KB 7.13s
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #That path is from the XDG Desktop Portal document portal, not a normal directory on your
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #disk.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #`/run/user/1000/doc/...` is a FUSE mount created by `xdg-document-portal`, part of
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #`xdg-desktop-portal`. It is used to give sandboxed applications (Flatpak, Snap, etc.)
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #access to files outside their sandbox without granting them full filesystem access.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- `/run/user/1000` is your user’s runtime directory (1000 is your UID).
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- `/doc` is the document portal mount.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- `ngHfyfxv_kKn8we9BMHIAQ` is a random document ID generated for one specific file access.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- `warren.png` is the file that was shared with the sandboxed app.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #So when a Flatpak app (like a browser, image viewer, or editor) opens a file via a file chooser,
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #the portal exposes that file at a path like this. The app can read it, but it cannot see the rest
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #of your home directory unless you grant it.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #Key points:
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- It is temporary: it disappears when the session ends or when the document is closed.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- It is not a copy: it is a live view of the original file via FUSE.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- It is safe: only your user and the sandboxed app can access it.
2a1bc5a2 [deepseek-flash] #- The real file is wherever you originally opened it from (e.g., `~/Pictures/warren.png`).
2a1bc5a3 [deepseek-flash] #
2a1bc5a3 [deepseek-flash] #If you want to find the original file while the path still exists, you can often use `lsof` on the
2a1bc5a3 [deepseek-flash] #portal process or just copy the file from that path to a normal location.
2a1bc5a3 [deepseek-flash] #
