2ad53ff6 [skid@archlinux] approches to mining novel correlations
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-4-argon 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 8.894KB 25.00s
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #Mining novel correlations—especially across vast, heterogeneous datasets—requires moving beyond
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #traditional linear statistics. Modern approaches combine classical data mining, graph theory,
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #topological analysis, and frontier AI models to uncover non-obvious, non-linear, and cross-domain
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #relationships.
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #Here is a breakdown of the primary approaches to discovering novel correlations:
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #1. Literature-Based Discovery (LBD) & The "Swanson Linking" Paradigm
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #Originally pioneered by Don Swanson, this approach looks for "undiscovered public knowledge" by
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #finding indirect connections across siloed bodies of literature.
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #• ABC Model: If Domain 1 establishes that Concept A influences Concept B, and Domain 2
2ad54192 [gemini-4-argon] #establishes that Concept B influences Concept C, an LBD system flags a potential novel correlation
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #between A and C, even if no single paper has ever mentioned them together.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #• Modern Execution: Frontier language models are used to extract structured entities and
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #relationships (triplets) from millions of unstructured papers, patents, and clinical trials to
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #automate this bridging process at scale.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #2. Knowledge Graph Link Prediction & Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #Once data is structured as a network of nodes (entities) and edges (relationships), discovering a
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #novel correlation becomes a topological problem of link prediction.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #• Graph Embeddings: Algorithms like Node2Vec or TransE project nodes into a
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #high-dimensional vector space based on their network neighborhood. Nodes that share structural
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #roles will cluster together, suggesting hidden equivalences.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #• GNNs: Graph Neural Networks pass messages between connected nodes to learn complex,
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #multi-hop relational patterns, predicting the probability that a missing edge (a novel correlation)
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #should exist between two distant nodes.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #3. Latent Space Alignment & Cross-Modal Embeddings
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #Deep learning models compress complex data into dense vector representations (embeddings). By
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #analyzing the geometry of these latent spaces, researchers can find correlations that are invisible
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #in raw data.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #• Vector Arithmetic & Cosine Similarity: In a shared embedding space, concepts from
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #completely different domains (e.g., a material's crystal structure and a textual description of
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #superconductivity) might map to nearby coordinates, revealing candidate materials before physical
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #testing.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #• Contrastive Learning (CLIP-style architectures): Training models to align different
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #modalities—such as genomic sequences, cellular microscopy images, and patient clinical notes—allows
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #the system to discover how a subtle visual cellular anomaly correlates with a specific genetic
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #mutation.
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54193 [gemini-4-argon] #4. Non-Linear Information-Theoretic Measures
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #Traditional metrics like Pearson’s r only capture linear relationships. To mine complex datasets
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #without assuming a specific functional form, information theory is used.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Mutual Information (MI): Measures how much knowing one variable reduces uncertainty about
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #another, capturing any relationship (linear, exponential, sinusoidal, etc.).
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Maximal Information Coefficient (MIC): Specifically designed for rapid exploration of
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #massive datasets, MIC applies a grid to scatter plots of variable pairs to find the highest mutual
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #information, scoring relationships equally regardless of how noisy or non-linear they are.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Distance Correlation: Unlike classical correlation, distance correlation is zero if
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #and only if the random variables are statistically independent, making it highly reliable for
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #catching complex dependencies.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #5. Causal Discovery & Structural Equation Modeling
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #Correlation is famously not causation, and high-dimensional datasets are plagued by spurious
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #correlations. Causal discovery algorithms attempt to mine the actual underlying data-generating
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #mechanism.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Constraint-Based Algorithms (e.g., PC Algorithm, FCI): Use conditional independence tests
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #to systematically prune away indirect associations, leaving behind a skeleton of direct
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #relationships (a Directed Acyclic Graph, or DAG), even in the presence of unmeasured confounding
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #variables.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Granger Causality & Transfer Entropy: Used in time-series data (such as neuroscience or
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #macroeconomics) to determine if historical changes in Variable X provide statistically significant
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #information about future changes in Variable Y beyond Y's own history.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #6. Topological Data Analysis (TDA)
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #When relationships involve interactions between three, four, or dozens of variables simultaneously,
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #pairwise correlation matrices fail. TDA looks at the "shape" of high-dimensional data.
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #• Persistent Homology: Identifies topological features (connected components, loops, voids)
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #in data point clouds that persist across multiple scales. This has been used in oncology to
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #identify entirely new subgroups of breast cancer patients that share subtle, multi-variable genetic
2ad54194 [gemini-4-argon] #profiles.
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #• Mapper Algorithm: Converts high-dimensional data into a simplified network graph,
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #allowing researchers to visually and algorithmically spot "flares" or branches representing
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #anomalous subpopulations with unique variable correlations.
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #7. Symbolic Regression & Mechanistic Discovery
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #Instead of fitting data to a pre-selected model (like linear or logistic regression) or a black-box
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #neural network, symbolic regression searches the space of mathematical expressions to find the
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #exact equation governing the data.
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #• Genetic Programming & Physics-Informed Neural Networks (PINNs): These systems combine
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #mathematical operators (+, -, ×, \div, \sin, \exp) and evolve them to fit empirical data, balancing
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #accuracy against equation complexity (Occam's razor). This approach has successfully rediscovered
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #physical laws from raw sensor data and uncovered new governing equations in fluid dynamics and
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #astrophysics.
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #8. Agentic Hypothesis Generation & In-Silico Abduction
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #The newest approach utilizes frontier LLMs not just as passive embedding engines, but as active
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #reasoning agents.
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #• Multi-Agent Debate & Synthesis: Separate AI agents are assigned domain personas (e.g., an
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #immunologist, a biophysicist, and a statistician) and tasked with reviewing anomalous statistical
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #outputs. By cross-examining each other's domain knowledge, they filter out artifacts and propose
2ad54195 [gemini-4-argon] #plausible mechanistic hypotheses for why a novel correlation exists.
