2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #Reasoning Summary
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #I am reviewing the shared `relay.ts` source file to see how the `reasonoutloud` flag and Gemini API
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #integrations are currently implemented, as well as checking for any potential issues or recent
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #updates in the harness.
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #Observations on `relay.ts` (v2.0.4)
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #1. `reasonoutloud` Handling across Endpoints:
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #   * Chat Completions (DeepSeek / OpenAI-compatible): In `relay()`, the harness checks
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #`choice.message.reasoning_content` and prints it inside a `=== reasoning ===` block when
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #`roha.config.reasonoutloud` is true.
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #   * Responses API (`v1/responses`): It iterates through `response.output` chunks of type
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #`"reasoning"` and echoes each item in `chunk.summary` prefixed with `[REASON]`.
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #   * Google Generative AI (`connectGoogle`) & Anthropic (`connectAnthropic`): Currently,
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #the custom completion wrappers for Gemini and Anthropic do not extract or map thought/reasoning
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #parts into `choice.message.reasoning_content` (though `connectGoogle` does account for
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #`usage.thoughtsTokenCount` in `completion_tokens`). If you are testing `reasonoutloud` with Gemini
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #models that return thought parts via the SDK, they may be merged into `result.response.text()` or
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #omitted unless explicitly extracted from `candidate.content.parts`.
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #2. Gemini Tool Call Formatting (`geminiToolCalls`):
2ad56f3a [gemini-4-argon] #   * In `connectGoogle`, `geminiToolCalls` was updated to return objects with `thought_signature`
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #and `function_call` properties instead of the standard OpenAI `id`, `type`, and `function: { name,
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #arguments }` structure (which is now in `oldGeminiToolCalls`).
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #   * However, downstream in `relay()` and `processToolCalls()`, the harness expects `tool.id` and
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #`tool.function.name` / `tool.function.arguments`. If Gemini triggers a tool call,
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #`processToolCalls` may reject it as `"Invalid tool call format"` unless `oldGeminiToolCalls` is
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #used or `processToolCalls` is updated to handle both formats.
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #3. Minor Code Hygiene Notes:
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #   * In `starCommand`, there is a reference to `shareList` (`if(isFinite(name) &&
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #shareList?.length)`), which was deprecated and replaced by `sortedShares`.
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #   * In `callCommand`, there is a stray empty template literal ```` `` ```` right after `try {`.
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #Please let me know if you would like to focus on any specific part of the harness or test a
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #particular feature.
2ad56f3b [gemini-4-argon] #
