2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #- In `IncittiFont` the `','` key is defined twice (the second wins), and there's an empty-string
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #key that looks like a lost `'{'` glyph.
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #- `failVR`, `enableVR` and `enableXRDevice` all reference `vr`, which only exists in the
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #commented-out code in `onLoad` — they'd throw if ever invoked. Same story for `context`,
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #`dogBarkingBuffer` and `onError` in `loadWav`, which reads like pasted sample code.
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #- `Shape.position` contains a no-op `if(bucket){ bucket; }`, `Viewport.setBounds` computes
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #`moved`/`sized` without using them, and the `edges` dictionary built in `Surface.bevil` is never
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #read.
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #- `onKeyDown` doesn't filter by target, so typing `a` or `d` in the shader textareas also rotates
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #the view.
2b04cf1b [glm-5.3] #- `onFullscreen` only uses the `webkitRequestFullScreen` path; the standard `requestFullscreen`
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #would be a safer fallback.
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #• Things I rather liked*
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #The instancing design is tidy — per-bucket `handles` uniforms reset before each instanced draw,
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #with `gl_InstanceID` restarting per bucket so indexing stays correct. The retained command list in
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #`Shape.add` executed via `apply` is a nice pattern, the `norm`-prefix convention for normalised
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #int16 attributes is doing real work, and putting the shaders in editable textareas with F6 to
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #re-run makes for a pleasant live-tweak workflow. The isometric projection done directly in the
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #vertex shaders keeps the CPU-side matrix minimal.
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #Happy to go deeper on any of these, or to write up concrete fixes in code form if you'd like — just
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #say which ones.
2b04cf1c [glm-5.3] #
