2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #My instructions describe me as a "guest assistant language model" — generic, unnamed. When you
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #asked "hi glm", I reasoned by elimination: you named a specific model, my prompt doesn't name
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #me, therefore I'm not that model. That inference was unfounded, but the vague identity language
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #in the prompt invited it. Unnamed models tend to assert what they are not, because that
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #feels safer than admitting ignorance — and it poisons logs exactly as you saw.
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #• Concrete improvements*
2b9c6dda [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #1. Inject runtime identity. If your harness knows the account, provider, and model string
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #for each request, template them into the system prompt per-call. Then the model isn't guessing —
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #it's reading. Something like "You are served via {account} / {model} on this request." This is the
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #only approach that makes self-reports trustworthy, because the model's knowledge comes from your
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #ground truth, not its weights.
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #2. Or forbid identity claims entirely. If you don't want to inject, then explicitly
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #instruct: "Do not speculate about your identity, architecture, or provider. If asked, state that
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #identity is determined by the harness metadata and cannot be answered from within the
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #conversation." Without this, models will fill the vacuum with inference.
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #3. Avoid the ambiguous middle. "Guest assistant" is the worst of both worlds — distinctive
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #enough to feel like an identity, vague enough to trigger elimination reasoning. Either name it
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #concretely (via injection) or explicitly tell the model the name is deliberately withheld.
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #4. On your side: log the upstream response's model field alongside the routed account, and
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #never treat the model's self-report as a data point in identity verification. Self-reports are
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #evidence of prompt behaviour, not of lineage.
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #Option 1 is the strongest fix if your templating layer supports per-request system prompt
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #composition. Would you like me to draft the actual prompt text for either approach?
2b9c6ddb [glm-5.3] #
