2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.006 66.66KB 28.82s
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #Read through all four. Comments below are limited to what looks new or inconsistent, plus a few
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #things the failures in `notes.md` point at.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #Documentation inconsistencies
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- Log file naming conflicts. `README.md` says a project owns `~/relay.log`, but `forge.md`
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #`/files` documents `history.log` as "per project relay logging". One of the two is stale.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- `agents.md` is referenced but not documented. `/share` says "See forge files section for
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #treatment of 'agents.md', 'history.log' and 'relay.md'", yet the `/files` section only covers
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #`relay.md` and `history.log`. The `agents.md` behaviour is missing.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- Provider status is inconsistent across three lists. The setup env list still includes
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #`MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `ALIBABA_API_KEY` and `COHERE_API_KEY` while the deprecated section retires
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #those SDKs; conversely `HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY` and `MOONSHOT_API_KEY` appear in setup but in neither
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #the supported nor the deprecated list. Worth collapsing to one authoritative table.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- `/files` opening sentence is truncated — "Certain files when shared" has no predicate.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- History section link mislabelled: the fourth stage reads
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #`[forge](https://github.com/nitrologic/fountain)`, duplicating the third stage's label.
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #- Roadmap vs config drift: roadmap lists "persona and agents.md addition plan", but
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #`persona` is already config item 23 and the notes todo still says "persona - named system prompt
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #mods".
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #The `/drop` failure is reproducible from your own log
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #The `/drop` listing and the `/share` listing disagree on both size and index for the same files
2ba78dee [deepseek-flash] #(`437` / `166` vs `2.3K` / `5.6K`), and after `[DROP] share: share776` reports success the next
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #`/share` still shows four entries. That pattern suggests `/drop` is rendering from a cached history
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #snapshot rather than live share state, and that the removal is acting on something other than the
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #list `/share` prints — consistent with `roha.keyedShares[key] = roha.sharedFiles` aliasing the
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #array, so the drop either mutates a copy or the project restore re-appends on the following
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #`/share`.
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #Every empty-message 400 follows a `/commit`
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #All five "the message at position N with role 'user' must not be empty" errors in the notes occur
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #immediately after `/commit`, never after a plain `/push` or `/say`. That strongly implicates the
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #commit path emitting a zero-length user entry — plausibly a deleted or unreadable share, or a
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #zero-byte file. A guard that substitutes a short placeholder (or skips the entry) when the
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #committed content is empty would remove the whole class of failure.
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #The prompt report's `size` is not a predictor of request size
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #You have a 400 at 102 MB against a 16 MB limit, and a 429 requesting 25.6 M tokens against a 4 M
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #TPM limit, while the report line above the same exchange reads `679.0KB`. The `size` figure is raw
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #file bytes; the wire payload is base64 (~4/3) plus full history plus the tool blocks. Adding an
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #encoded-bytes and token estimate to the report would let you see the failure coming rather than
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #discovering it from the vendor error.
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #`includeThoughts`
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #The Gemini exchange is useful: the config was accepted and a `thoughtSignature` came back, but the
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #candidate contained no thought part — so `includeThoughts: true` only yields visible reasoning when
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #the model actually reasons on that turn, which this prompt did not. Two implications worth
2ba78def [deepseek-flash] #verifying in the relay:
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #1. The `thoughtSignature` must be preserved in the assistant history and echoed on the next turn;
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #dropping it degrades multi-turn reasoning on that family.
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #2. `temperature = grokTemperature` in the Gemini request builder is a naming leak from the xAI
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #path. Harmless at runtime, but it will mislead you while debugging which provider's temperature is
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #being applied.
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #Two smaller things
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #- `replaceShortCodes` resolves `./shortcode.json` against the process CWD. Forge has `/cd`, and the
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #invoke script `pushd`s into the relay directory, so shortcode substitution silently breaks the
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #moment the working directory moves. Resolving against `import.meta.url` and loading once at module
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #init would make it CWD-independent. The pattern `:([a-z_]+):` also misses digits, uppercase and
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #`:+1:`-style codes.
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #- If a slopmark is a HEX32 count of sixteenths, the counter exhausts 2^32/16 ≈ 268 M seconds ≈ 8.5
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #years after 2025-04-12, i.e. late 2033. Fine if the timestamp is advisory, but `/save` naming
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #(`transmission-HEX32_TIME.json`) would collide on rollover — worth a note in the README either way.
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #Structural note
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #`notes.md` is now 53.8 KB and mixes live transcripts, vendor reference material (Godot `ClassDB`,
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #xAI voice list, websearch snippets), and open bug notes. Since it's shared into every model's
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #context, splitting the reference blocks into a separate file would cut a large fixed cost per
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #request without losing anything.
2ba78df0 [deepseek-flash] #
