2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.031 287.0KB 125.95s
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #Reviewed the new `relay.ts`, `relaybot.ts`, `slopprompt.ts`, `slopsearch.ts` and `client.ts`, plus
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #the `forge.md` edit. Comments on what changed, then the defects that stand out.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #Documentation
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #`/files` now says `forge.log` instead of `history.log` — that resolves the naming conflict I
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #flagged last time, but the `/share` section below it still points at `"agents.md", "history.log"
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #and "relay.md"`, so the stale name survives in the one place a reader is sent to look. `agents.md`
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #is still undocumented.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #More significant: several documented commands have no handler in `callCommand` at all.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #- `/project [drop] [key]` and config flag 20 `project` — no `case "project"`. The
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #`keyedShares`/`setProject` machinery is commented out in `addShare` and `commitShares`, so the
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #README claim that "/share of a relay.md keys a project to that folder name" describes behaviour
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #that isn't in this build. The transcript in the earlier share (`[KEY] loadProject elfutil`) is from
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #1.9.x.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #- `/files` — documented, no handler.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #- `/history` and `/list` are presented as synonyms for a conversation summary, but `list` calls
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #`listHistory` and `history` calls `readHistory`, which parses log files and reports per-day tag
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #byte counts. Very different commands.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #Conversely `persona`, `tex`, `spec`, `sys` and `announce` are implemented and undocumented.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #`/think` documents a 0–8192 budget, but `grokThink` is only emitted when `info.pricing.length > 3`,
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #which reads as a proxy for "supports thinking" — so `/think` is silently inert for most models.
2ba7a318 [deepseek-flash] #`/say` is documented as taking "previous or specified text" but ignores its arguments. `/drop`
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #still says "drop all files" while the implementation is per-index.
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #Config descriptions have also drifted: flag 3 is "enable model websearch tool interface" in
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`forge.md` and "enable search tool interface" in `flagNames`; flag 13 differs similarly. And
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`relayVersion` is now `2.0.6` while the README badge says `2.0.5`.
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #Configuration defaults are not merged
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`readForge` replaces `roha.config` wholesale with the parsed JSON. Any flag absent from an existing
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`forge.json` is `undefined`, not the `emptyConfig` default. That is not cosmetic: `syncRelay`
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #defaults true but resolves falsy, so an older forge silently takes the `else` branch into
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`beginRelay` — the WIP async path that pushes a literal `"completion ready"` into history. Same for
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`thinking`, `listen` and `project`. `emptyConfig` also omits `search` and `persona` entirely, so
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #their documented defaults never apply even on a fresh forge.
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #Related: `ConfigFlags` declares `persona: string`, but it is toggled as a boolean by `/config` and
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #tested as a boolean in the `responses` path. And `budget` is typed as the literal `false`, so
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #assigning `true` is a type error.
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #Persistence
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #`writeForge` builds `json` and then assigns `roha.model = grokModel` before writing `json` — the
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #assignment happens after serialisation, so the selected model is never actually saved. The next
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #boot falls back to `defaultModel`.
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #Bugs with immediate consequences
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a319 [deepseek-flash] #- `announceCommand` iterates `for (const connection of slopConnections)` on a `Map`, so
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`connection` is a `[key, value]` pair; `connection?.write` is undefined and the call throws. It
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #needs `.values()`.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `open(...)` is called in `geminiSay`, `gptSay` and the speech branch of `relay`, but nothing
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #named `open` is imported or defined — only `openCommand` and `openWithDefaultApp` exist. Those
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #three TTS paths should throw `ReferenceError`.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `geminiToolCalls` emits `{thought_signature, function_call:{name, args}}` and assigns that to
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`message.tool_calls`, but `relay` and `processToolCalls` both expect `{id, type, function:{name,
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #arguments}}`. `tool.function.name` will throw on the first Gemini function call. The commented-out
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`oldGeminiToolCalls` produces the correct shape.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `anthropicMessages` switches on `user` and `assistant` only — there is no `tool` case, so tool
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #results are discarded and any tool loop sends `tool_use` with no matching `tool_result`.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `multiHistory` and `strictHistory` push user content unconditionally, whereas `plainHistory`
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #guards with `if (item.content)`. An empty shared file therefore produces `{type:"text", text:""}`
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #and explains the recurring "the message at position N with role 'user' must not be empty" after
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`/commit`. `strictHistory` also forwards tool items verbatim via `{...item}`, including the
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #internal `title` field.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `plainHistory` computes `role` from the model-name comparison and then never uses it; the
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #assistant branch pushes `role:"assistant"` regardless. The comment "assistant role only when
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #model==mut" describes behaviour that isn't happening.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `stripShare(share)` ignores its argument and rewrites every `content`/`image` item in history. In
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`commitShares`, `starshare` calls it for each starless share — so one starless share strips the
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #entire context. Additionally, starless shares hit `continue` before `validShares.push`, so if any
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #share is removed in the same pass, `roha.sharedFiles = validShares` silently deletes them from the
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #project.
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #- `starCommand` references `shareList`, which no longer exists (the declaration is commented out) —
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`/star <index>` throws into `callCommand`'s catch. Separately, `listShares` sets `sortedShares` to
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #an array of id strings while `listShare` sets it to share objects, so `dropCommand`'s
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`findIndex(item => item.id === id)` compares a string to an object after a `/share` listing. And
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #`listShare` increments its display counter only for files that still exist, so the printed index
2ba7a31a [deepseek-flash] #and the array index diverge exactly when a file is missing — which is when you'd want to drop it.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- `unitString` declares `const unit` and then does `if (unit > 4) unit = 4`, which throws for
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #values ≥ 10^15. `Math.log10` of a value below 1 also yields a negative index into `units`.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- `load` does `rohaHistory = load`, but `loadHistory` returns `undefined` after calling
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #`resetHistory()` on a parse error. A corrupt save leaves `rohaHistory` undefined and the next relay
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #throws.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- `/model next` returns `nextActiveModel()`, an un-awaited Promise, from `modelCommand`;
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #`modelList.includes(promise)` is false, so the command falls through and just lists models.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- `shareGlob` calls `shareDir(entry.path, tag, 1, depth)` with `tag` undeclared. It is reachable
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #from the startup argument path.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- Both guards in `chat` read `if (!line.startsWith("//") || !line.startsWith("/"))` — a string
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #cannot start with both, so the condition is always true. It should be `&&`. As written, a command
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #typed at a list prompt is fed back as an index, and `creditCommand` swallows any input.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #- In the legacy completions path, `usage` is only guarded at `const spent = usage ? ...`; the later
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #`usage.prompt_tokens` and `usage.cache_tokens` are unguarded, so a provider that omits usage
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #crashes the relay.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #Billing inconsistency between paths
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #`bumpModel` charges uncached input at the full rate and cached input at the cache rate. The inlined
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #copy in the completions path charges `spent[0]  tokenRate` (which already includes cached
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #tokens) plus `cached  cacheRate` — cached tokens are billed twice. Since the
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #duplication was flagged earlier and `bumpModel` now exists, routing the legacy path through it
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #would fix both the duplication and the arithmetic.
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #Size accounting
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #`MaxFileSize` is 16 MB per file, but the request body is base64 (~4/3) plus the blob metadata item
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #plus the full history. That is consistent with the two failures in your notes: 102 MB against
2ba7a31b [deepseek-flash] #Kimi's 16 MB total-message cap, and 25.6 M tokens against a 4 M TPM cap, both while the prompt
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #report showed a small `size`. A per-request budget check — encoded bytes and an estimated token
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #count — before dispatch would surface these locally rather than as vendor errors.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #Path handling
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #`forgePath` is absolute, but `listSaves`, `loadHistory("forge/" + save)`, `fetch_file` and
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #`historyCommand`'s archive path are all relative to `Deno.cwd()`. Since `/cd` changes the working
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #directory mid-session, `/save` then `/load` can write to one place and read from another.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #`fileType` also splits on `"/"` only, so `commonTextFiles` detection fails for Windows paths.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #relaybot.ts
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #- `readSystem()` is called in the main loop but never defined; `initSystem` resolves with no value,
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #so the `result == null` break fires rather than the system branch.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #- Three separate SIGINT listeners are registered (`initSystem`, its inner promise, and the
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #module-level one).
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #- `fountainDecoder` is a non-streaming `TextDecoder`, so a multi-byte character split across two
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #reads is corrupted. `slopprompt.ts` has the same class of problem in `processUtf8`, which slices a
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #fixed `bytesNeeded` from the current chunk and drops the byte on underflow.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #- `sloppyInfo[botName]` is dereferenced without a guard, so an unknown bot name fails at banner
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #construction.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #- `channel.send(chunk)` is not awaited inside the loop, so rate-limit rejections become unhandled.
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #client.ts
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #`quit()` sends `"quit"` and then the socket closes, which triggers `onClose` and reconnects a
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #second later — there is no shutdown flag, so the client cannot exit. `readonly OPEN = 1` is
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #declared but the check uses `WebSocket.OPEN`. `onMessage` also echoes every inbound payload back to
2ba7a31c [deepseek-flash] #the server, which will loop if the server does the same.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #slopsearch.ts
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #The file executes a live `exa.search` at import with `EXA_API_KEY` possibly undefined, and the call
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #uses a top-level `text` option that the documentation further down explicitly says must be nested
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #inside `contents`. The rest is reference material in a comment block, so it reads as a scratch file
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #rather than a module.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #Smaller items
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `resetHistory` assigns `rohaHistory` from `rohaMihi` and then overwrites it unconditionally;
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #`rohaMihi` is dead.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `clearShares` and `dropShares` are never called; `resetCommand` clears `sharedFiles` but not
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #`attachedFiles`.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `textExtensions`, `imageExtensions`, `isWide`/`WideRanges`, `listenerPromise`,
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #`relayTaskPromise`, `formatValues`, `formatObject` and `oldGeminiToolCalls` are unused. `isWide`
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #and `isDoubleWidth` are duplicate tables that disagree (U+1FAA3 is double-width in one, not the
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #other).
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `echoWarning` uses style `"blink"`, but `ansiStyle` implements `blink1` and `blink2` only, so
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #warnings render unstyled.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `tag_slop`'s schema offers `code|session|share|lode`; the handler implements `code|tag|share`.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #Two enum values are unreachable and one handler branch is unreachable. `annotateCode` is a stub.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `addShare` computes a SHA-256 per file, but change detection in `commitShares` compares mtime
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #only, so a `git checkout` re-uploads everything.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- `fileType` returns `application/octet-stream` for unknown extensions, and `shareBlob` then labels
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #that content `"image"` — so `.onnx`, `.wav`, `.mp3` and similar are sent as image blocks in plain
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #mode and silently dropped in multi mode.
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #- Several async functions are annotated with non-Promise return types (`hashFile(): string`,
2ba7a31d [deepseek-flash] #`promptForge(): string`). These run fine under `deno run` because type checking is off, but `deno
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #check` would reject them — worth knowing if you ever wire it into CI.
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #- `openCommand` pushes an array into a `string[]` for the Windows branch, and `openWithDefaultApp`
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #invokes `start` without `cmd /c`. Both helpers also use `Deno.run`, which I believe is unavailable
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #in Deno 2 — worth verifying before relying on `/open` or `/say` on Windows.
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #Happy to go deeper on any one of these, or to look at the project-keying design if you want to
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #bring `/project` back rather than remove it from the manual.
2ba7a31e [deepseek-flash] #
