2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.010 524.6KB 24.12s
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #`relay.ts` is byte-identical to the previous share (137429 bytes, same length), so everything from
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #my last review still stands. I'll limit this to the documentation changes and the handful of code
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #findings I hadn't reached before.
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #What the doc edits fixed
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #- `/history` and `/list` are now described as distinct commands, which matches the code: `history`
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #parses `forge.log` into per-day tag byte counts, `list` reports per-entry size and cost from
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #`rohaHistory`.
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #- `/project` is gone from the manual, consistent with the commented-out `setProject`/`keyedShares`
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #machinery.
2ba7cd28 [deepseek-flash] #- Removing `/files` is defensible, but it leaves a dangling reference — see below.
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #The flag index table is now wrong from 20 onwards
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #This is the most consequential result of removing the project feature. `flagNames` has 24 entries
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #(indices 0–23); `forge.md` still lists 25 (0–24) because `project` is still in the table.
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #Everything from 20 shifts by one:
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #╭───────┬─────────────┬─────────────────────────╮
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  Doc  │  Doc says   │  Code actually toggles  │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #├───────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────┤
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  20   │  project    │  thinking               │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  21   │  thinking   │  underline              │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  22   │  underline  │  persona                │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  23   │  persona    │  starshare              │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #│  24   │  starshare  │  nothing                │
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #╰───────┴─────────────┴─────────────────────────╯
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #`/config 24` falls through `flag in flagNames` with no else branch, so it fails silently. `/config
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #20` silently turns thinking on. Since `persona` is a string in `ConfigFlags`, `/config 22` also
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #flips it between `false` and `true`, which is not a persona name.
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #Dangling reference, and a third log filename
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #`/share` still reads "See forge files section for treatment of "agents.md", "relay.log" and
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #"relay.md" files when shared." There is no longer a files section, `agents.md` has never been
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #documented, and `relay.log` is the third name for a log that the code writes as `forge.log`. So the
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #log has now appeared as `history.log`, `relay.log` and `forge.log` across successive revisions of
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #these two files. Worth settling on one name before the next pass.
2ba7cd29 [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #README
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- Version badge and heading still say 2.0.5; `relayVersion` is 2.0.6.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- Roadmap still lists "relay.ts project support - final testing" after the feature was removed.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- The setup env list still includes `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `ALIBABA_API_KEY` and `COHERE_API_KEY` while
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #the deprecated section retires those SDKs, and `HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY`/`MOONSHOT_API_KEY` still
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #appear in setup but in neither the supported nor the deprecated list.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- History section still links the fourth stage with the label `forge`, duplicating the third stage.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #New code findings
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- `squashMessages` mutates live history. It pushes the original item references into
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #`squashed` and then does `last.content += "\n" + current.content`. `/log` calls it with
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #`rohaHistory` directly when `config.squash` is set, so a single `/log` permanently concatenates
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #entries in the real history. It needs shallow copies per item.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- `slopFrames` is undeclared. The slops worker handler calls
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #`slopFrames.push(payload.frame)` on a `tick` event, but no `slopFrames` is declared anywhere.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #Latent only because `config.slops` defaults false, but it will throw on the first frame when
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #enabled.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- `MaxFileSize` can never be sent. It evaluates to exactly 16777216 (16 MiB), which equals
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #Kimi's total-message cap quoted in your notes. Base64 alone is ~22.4 MB for a file at that limit,
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #before blob metadata and history. A per-file cap of roughly 11 MB, or a check on the encoded
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #request size, would prevent the guaranteed failure.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- `geminiSay` hardcodes the account key `rohaEndpoint["gemini"]`. Every other provider
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #lookup derives the key from the model name. If the account is named `google` in `accounts.json`,
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #`/say` throws on a missing endpoint rather than reporting a configuration error.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- Unawaited `resetModel` at startup. The module-level call is not awaited, so its internal
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #`writeForge` from `aboutModel` races the later `writeForge` calls in the boot sequence.
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #- `keyedShares` is now dead state that survives in `emptyRoha`, `readForge`, `resetCommand`
2ba7cd2a [deepseek-flash] #and the commented-out lines in `addShare`/`commitShares`, so it will keep being serialised into
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #`forge.json`. `shareName()` is likewise unused now that the `setProject` call is commented out.
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #Still outstanding from the previous review and unaffected by these edits: the empty-user-message
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #400s from `strictHistory`/`multiHistory`, the Gemini tool-call shape mismatch, the missing `tool`
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #case in `anthropicMessages`, `announceCommand` iterating Map entries, the undefined `open()`,
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #`starCommand`'s reference to the removed `shareList`, the `||` that should be `&&` in the two
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #`chat` guards, and the unmerged config defaults.
2ba7cd2b [deepseek-flash] #
